:"sha256:34f75ad0652e00af00748fada4ead319296a17f9df0e4cf2a70f6720a3527449","file":"preprints/Sharp-One-Third-Stability-of-Brenier-Maps-September-25-2026/build/source/sections/introduction.tex","line":31,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"b2d45acab4b2aa1eaac7556922812d78f539e13089d75a6270f2ebe5f2cdf275","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Sharp-One-Third-Stability-of-Brenier-Maps-September-25-2026/build/source/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:34f75ad0652e00af00748fada4ead319296a17f9df0e4cf2a70f6720a3527449","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Sharp-One-Third-Stability-of-Brenier-Maps-September-25-2026/build/source/sections/introduction.tex#L31"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{main:stability}\nFor every \\(K,Y\\) as above there is a finite constant \\(C(K,Y)\\) such that\n\\[\n \\|T_\\mu-T_\\nu\\|_{L^2(\\rho)}\n \\le C(K,Y)\\,W_2(\\mu,\\nu)^{1/3}\n \\qquad\\bigl(\\mu,\\nu\\in\\Prob(Y)\\bigr).\n\\]\nThe targets may be atomic, singular, or absolutely continuous. The\nexponent \\(1/3\\) cannot be replaced by any larger exponent in general,\neven for \\(K=Y=[-1,1]^d\\) and targets with exactly three atoms."}
